<title>UK: Nigerian March exports normal despite output cut - Shell.</title>
<headline>Nigerian March exports normal despite output cut - Shell.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Nigeria said on Monday it would be able to meet all of its March export commitments despite a 100,000 barrels per day (bpd) cut in production caused by the weekend shutdown of five pumping stations in the Niger delta.  </p>
<p>The five flow stations, which feed the Forcados export stream, were shut down on Saturday after they were overrun by local villagers.</p>
<p>&quot;This will not affect exports for the rest of this month,&quot; head of exports for Shell Nigeria Captain A.G. Dewit told Reuters by telephone.</p>
<p>Dewit said a prolonged closure could have an impact on exports in April.</p>
<p>Shell has capacity to store about five million barrels of crude oil at the Forcados export terminal.</p>
<p>-- Mark Thompson, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
</text>
